    "problem_statement": "Language fallback function broken due to variable scope issue\n\n#### Description\n\nThe deprecated language fallback functionality is not working properly. When using deprecated language codes, the function fails to access the `deprecated` dictionary variable, causing an `UnboundLocalError`.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom gtts import gTTS\n\n# Try using a deprecated language code\ntts = gTTS(text='Hello world', lang='zh-cn')  # zh-cn is deprecated, should fallback to zh-CN\n```\n\nThis should trigger a deprecation warning and fallback to the correct language code, but instead raises:\n\n```\nUnboundLocalError: local variable 'deprecated' referenced before assignment\n```\n\nThe same issue occurs when trying to use any deprecated language codes like 'es-es', 'es-us', 'zh-tw', etc."
  }
